<title>BELGIUM: Tietmeyer wants lira at 970 to mark - source.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer wants lira at 970 to mark - source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank chief Hans Tietmeyer wants the Italian lira to join the Exchange Rate Mechanism at the rate of 970 to the German mark and opposes a weaker rate, an diplomat said.</p>
<p>&quot;Tietmeyer wants 970,&quot; the diplomat told reporters during a ministerial meeting in Brussels on the issue. &quot;He wants a strong lira.&quot;  </p>
<p>Italy has signalled it wants to enter the ERM at a weaker rate, at at least 1,000 to the mark, but the majority of EU countries were opposing that.</p>
<p>Top EU monetary officials were negotiating the lira's re-entry into the monetary grid since midday.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
